      "writtenOn": "2020-05-20T09:56:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is briefly described in TCPCI Spec - Section (4.4.5.4.2 Automatic Sink Discharge by the TCPC after a Disconnect (normative)).\n\nThis mainly depends if there is a difference between PPC and TCPC between these three values:\n* VBUS_SINK_DISCONNECT_THRESHOLD\n* vSafe5V\n* vSafe0v\n\nThere is an \"allowed range\" for each of those values, and specific implementations can pick any value within it. Assuming those values are roughly syncrhonized, no, I expect no ill affects from \"discharging too fast\".\n\nThe only concern emerges if both are on, and we get state desynch. And one gets \"stuck on\" for some reason. Depending on discharge resistor value programmed, various effects could occur. But that is purely hypothetical.",
      "parentUuid": "325e22a1_1ab5f8ed",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "f7ce90a20d6d5412c0bcea828e90c0f8350b9aaa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
